  <h1>Lesson 12: Colors & Background in CSS</h1>
  <p>Learn color, background-color, HEX, RGB, RGBA, Opacity, Gradient & Background Image | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Test - 100 Marks</button>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Test is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the test or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. color vs background-color</h2>
    <p>These are the 2 most used color properties. Do not confuse them:</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Property</th><th>Changes</th><th>Example</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>color</b></td><td>Text color</td><td>color: red;</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>background-color</b></td><td>Box background color</td><td>background-color: blue;</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">red</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Text becomes red */</span><br>
<span class="tag">div</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">background-color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">blue</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Box becomes blue */</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><h3 style="color:#dc2626;margin:0">This text is Red - color: red;</h3><div style="background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:8px;text-align:center">This box is Blue - background-color: blue;</div></div>
    <h2>2. 3 Ways to Write a Color</h2>
    <p>There are 3 ways to write a color in CSS. All 3 give the same result. Real developers use <b>HEX</b> most.</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Way</th><th>Example</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>1. Name</b></td><td>red, blue, green</td><td>Simple English name - Only 140 colors</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>2. HEX</b></td><td>#FF0000, #2563eb</td><td># + 6 letters/numbers - Millions of colors</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>3. RGB</b></td><td>rgb(255, 0, 0)</td><td>Red, Green, Blue - Each 0 to 255</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">red</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#FF0000</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Same red */</span><br>
<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">rgb(255, 0, 0)</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Same red */</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result - Same Red in 3 Ways:</b><div class="color-row"><div class="color-box" style="background:#dc2626">Name<br>red</div><div class="color-box" style="background:#FF0000">HEX<br>#FF0000</div><div class="color-box" style="background:rgb(255,0,0)">RGB<br>rgb(255,0,0)</div></div></div>
    <h2>3. Popular HEX Colors - Copy These</h2>
    <p>Use these HEX codes in your projects - they look professional:</p>
    <div class="result">
      <div class="color-row"><div class="color-box" style="background:#0f172a">#0f172a<br>Dark Navy</div><div class="color-box" style="background:#2563eb">#2563eb<br>Blue</div><div class="color-box" style="background:#16a34a">#16a34a<br>Green</div><div class="color-box" style="background:#dc2626">#dc2626<br>Red</div></div>
      <div class="color-row"><div class="color-box" style="background:#f59e0b">#f59e0b<br>Orange</div><div class="color-box" style="background:#7c3aed;color:white">#7c3aed<br>Purple</div><div class="color-box" style="background:#ec4899">#ec4899<br>Pink</div><div class="color-box" style="background:#64748b">#64748b<br>Grey</div></div>
      <div class="color-row"><div class="color-box" style="background:#ffffff;color:#222;border:1px solid #e2e8f0">#ffffff<br>White</div><div class="color-box" style="background:#000000">#000000<br>Black</div><div class="color-box" style="background:#f4f6f8;color:#222">#f4f6f8<br>Light Grey</div><div class="color-box" style="background:#e0f2fe;color:#222">#e0f2fe<br>Light Blue</div></div>
    </div>
    <h2>4. RGBA & Opacity - Transparent Color</h2>
    <p><b>RGBA</b> = Red, Green, Blue, <b>Alpha</b>. Alpha means transparency. 0 = Fully transparent, 1 = Fully solid.</p>
    <p><b>Opacity</b> = Makes the full box transparent. 0 = Invisible, 1 = Normal.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">div</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">background-color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.5)</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* 50% transparent blue */</span><br>
<span class="tag">img</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">opacity</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">0.5</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Image 50% faded */</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><div style="background:rgba(37,99,235,0.5);color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;margin:6px 0;text-align:center">RGBA - 50% Transparent Blue</div><div style="background:rgba(22,163,74,0.3);color:#222;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;margin:6px 0;text-align:center">RGBA - 30% Transparent Green</div><div style="background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;margin:6px 0;text-align:center;opacity:0.5">Opacity 0.5 - Full box is faded</div></div>
    <h2>5. Gradient - 2 Colors Mixed</h2>
    <p>Gradient mixes 2 colors together. Very popular for buttons and headers in modern websites.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">div</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">background</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">linear-gradient(90deg, blue, green)</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><div class="gradient-box">Blue → Green Gradient</div><div class="gradient-box2">Orange → Red Gradient</div></div>
    <h2>6. background-image - Image as Background</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">div</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">background-image</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">url("my-photo.jpg")</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">background-size</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">cover</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Image fills full box */</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">background-position</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">center</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">background-repeat</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">no-repeat</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><div style="background:#e0f2fe;border:2px dashed #2563eb;padding:25px;border-radius:10px;text-align:center;color:#2563eb;font-weight:bold">🖼️ Your Image Here as Background<br><span style="font-size:13px;color:#64748b">background-image: url("my-photo.jpg");</span></div></div>
    <h2>7. Full Example - Colourful Card</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;style&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">.card</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">background-color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#ffffff</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">#0f172a</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">padding</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">20px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">.btn</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">background</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">linear-gradient(90deg, #2563eb, #16a34a)</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">white</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/style&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><div style="background:white;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;text-align:center"><h3 style="color:#0f172a;margin:0">Ali Khan</h3><p style="color:#64748b;margin:5px 0">Web Developer</p><button class="btn" style="background:linear-gradient(90deg,#2563eb,#16a34a)">Contact Me</button></div></div>
    <h2>8. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>In Playground, make this:</p>
    <p>1. One <b>h1</b> with color <b>#2563eb</b><br>2. One <b>div</b> with background-color <b>#f59e0b</b><br>3. One <b>button</b> with gradient <b>blue → green</b></p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> color = Text color | background-color = Box color | 3 Ways = Name (red), HEX (#FF0000), RGB (rgb(255,0,0)) | RGBA = Transparent color, Alpha 0 to 1 | Opacity = Full box transparency | Gradient = linear-gradient(90deg, color1, color2) | background-image = url("photo.jpg")</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> After this lesson, go to <a href="/lesson13">Lesson 13 - Text Styling</a> to learn font-size, font-family, text-align, line-height and more.</p>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
    <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="showTest()">Go to Test → 📝</button>
    <div class="nav">
      <a class="btn btn-prev" href="/lesson11">← Lesson 11</a>
      <a id="nextLessonLink" class="btn btn-next" href="/lesson13">Next Lesson 13 →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

